# Sortable tables

Every data table in the app must support sorting via clickable column headers, matching the dashboard per-stock table pattern.

## Required pattern

1. Use `TableSortState` from `src/app/utils/table-sort.utils.ts` (do not duplicate sort logic).
2. Define a `columns` array with `{ key, label }` for each sortable column.
3. Expose a `sortedRows` computed that calls `tableSort.sort(rows, getValue)`.
4. Render headers with the shared `sort-btn` / `sort-btn-active` classes:

```html
<button type="button" class="sort-btn" [class.sort-btn-active]="tableSort.isActive(col.key)" (click)="tableSort.toggle(col.key, $event)">
  {{ col.label }} <span>{{ tableSort.indicator(col.key) }}</span>
</button>
```

5. Serial number (`#`) columns are not sortable.
6. Default sort: text columns ascending (`stockName`, `symbol`, `period`, dates); numeric columns descending (`netPnL`, `realisedPnL`, `amount`, etc.) — use `defaultSortDirection()`.

## Nested / accordion tables

Trade detail tables inside accordions must also be sortable using the same pattern (typically `tradeSort` with `sellDate` default).

## Do not

- Hard-code `.sort()` in templates without header toggles.
- Add new tables without sortable headers.
